    "text": "To determine how many muffins Janet bought, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money Janet spent on the muffins.\n2. Determine how many muffins she could buy with that amount of money.\n\nFirst, we know that Janet paid $20 and got $11 in change. Therefore, the total amount of money she spent on the muffins is:\n\\[ 20 - 11 = 9 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert the total amount spent from dollars to cents, since the price of each muffin is given in cents. There are 100 cents in a dollar, so:\n\\[ 9 \\text{ dollars} = 9 \\times 100 = 900 \\text{ cents} \\]\n\nEach muffin costs 75 cents, so the number of muffins Janet bought is:\n\\[ \\frac{900 \\text{ cents}}{75 \\text{ cents per muffin}} = 12 \\text{ muffins} \\]\n\nThus, the number of muffins Janet bought is:\n\\[ \\boxed{12} \\]",
